## 🛠️ Hardware Constraints & Implementation Notes

   1. Alternate Function (AF) Multi-Driven Safety:
   The assigned ports (such as PA11/PA12 for FDCAN1 and PA5/PA6/PA7 for SPI1) utilize non-overlapping alternate function matrices native to the STM32H7 chip layout. This guarantees zero pin-mux hardware conflicts when initializing registers via STMicroelectronics HAL/LL drivers.
   2. De-phase Sampling Rule:
   The ADC internal sampling registers must be configured to trigger ADC1, ADC2, and ADC3 sequentially with a forced 3-clock phase delay (De-phase Drive). This completely disperses internal silicon switching spikes, preventing cross-talk contamination onto sensor lines PC0 through PC3.
   3. Message RAM Partitioning:
   The SRAM designated for the FDCAN controllers must be hard-coded with non-overlapping offset boundaries in the firmware startup initialization files to prevent hardware bus-conflct locks during concurrent 1ms DMA writes.

